# The Boeing 747-400: JSBSim's B747 made to fly to its airport-planning document's
# and type certificate's figures (assets/figures/747-400.xml) by tools/make_747_400.py.
#
#   name TEXT...                 what it is called
#   model NAME                   its JSBSim model, in data/jsbsim/aircraft
#   start AIRSPEED_KT THROTTLE   a flight begun in the air: its calibrated
#                                airspeed, and the throttle that holds it
#
# Its published figures, if it has them, are data/figures/MODEL.xml, and its
# selftest's log data/selftest/MODEL.log (src/sim/catalogue.hpp).

name Boeing 747-400
model 747-400
class airliner
start 250 0.58
# The speedbrake lever works its speedbrakes or spoilers (src/sim/catalogue.hpp).
speedbrakes
# Her main tyres and brakes, for a wet runway's grip (docs/ASSETS.md):
# Boeing D6-58326-1 rev F, 7.2: H49x19.0-22 mains at 200 psi loaded, at
# 873,000-877,000 lb; Hydro-Aire's wheel-by-wheel brake system control unit.
brakes 200 fully-modulating
# Her CF6-80C2s' cascade thrust reversers, on all four (tools/make_747_400.py),
# and the reverse brought to idle at 60 kt, as Boeing's training manual has
# it (the 737-300's file says where; docs/ASSETS.md).
reversers 60
